      "text": "Medellín"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "939470184a1f8c4ecced625589d8cca742ce5752547474fb6d56f001f68b2a8d",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw9nvgw6-cx25ndvy",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, meet your English-speaking guide for a sightseeing tour of Medellín, the capital of Antioquia and one of Colombia’s largest cities.\n\nVisit the Museum of Antioquia and Plaza Botero, which displays sculptures by Fernando Botero. Then see the Palace of Culture and Veracruz Church, two of the city’s best-known historic landmarks.\n\nPart of the tour is dedicated to Comuna 13. Just a few years ago, it was considered one of Medellín’s most dangerous neighbourhoods. Today it is known for its street art, graffiti and cultural projects, and is one of the city’s most visited districts.\n\nNext, visit El Castillo Museum. Built in 1930, it is known for its decorative arts collection and gardens. After the tour, return to your hotel to relax."
    },
